{"id":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces#gt.lem5.9","title":"gt.lem5.9","path":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces.md","line":309,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces.tex#gt.lem5.9","uses":["[[references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces#gt.def5.3.compact-mapping]]","[[references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces#gt.def5.9.adjoint-hilbert]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces.tex","label":"gt.lem5.9","line":339,"source":"\\begin{lemma}\\label{gt.lem5.9}\\dcref{ch5:5.9}\\group{chapter-5}\n\\source{gilbarg-trudinger:page-0096}\n\n\\uses{gt.def5.3.compact-mapping,gt.def5.9.adjoint-hilbert}\nThe adjoint of a compact operator on a Hilbert space is compact.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\\source{gilbarg-trudinger:page-0096}\n\\sketch For bounded $x_j$, compactness supplies a Cauchy subsequence of\n$TT^*x_j$. The identity\n\\[\n\\|T^*(x_j-x_k)\\|^2=(x_j-x_k,TT^*(x_j-x_k))\n\\]\nthen makes $T^*x_j$ Cauchy.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section><span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-67742e6c656d352e39\"></span><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch5:5.9</span></span>\\group chapter-5 <span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">gilbarg-trudinger:page-0096</span></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FGilbargTrudinger%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fch05-banach-hilbert-spaces%23gt.def5.3.compact-mapping\">↗ gt.def5.3.compact-mapping</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FGilbargTrudinger%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fch05-banach-hilbert-spaces%23gt.def5.9.adjoint-hilbert\">↗ gt.def5.9.adjoint-hilbert</a> The adjoint of a compact operator on a Hilbert space is compact.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">gilbarg-trudinger:page-0096</span></span> \\sketch For bounded <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x_j$\">$x_j$</span>, compactness supplies a Cauchy subsequence of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$TT^*x_j$\">$TT^*x_j$</span>. The identity </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\| T^*(x_j-x_k)\\| ^2=(x_j-x_k,TT^*(x_j-x_k))  \\]\">\\[  \\| T^*(x_j-x_k)\\| ^2=(x_j-x_k,TT^*(x_j-x_k))  \\]</span></p><p> then makes <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T^*x_j$\">$T^*x_j$</span> Cauchy. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: group、sketch"]},"previous":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces#gt.eq5.12","next":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces#gt.lem5.10","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces#gt.def5.3.compact-mapping","title":"gt.def5.3.compact-mapping","label":"gt.def5.3.compact-mapping"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces#gt.def5.9.adjoint-hilbert","title":"gt.def5.9.adjoint-hilbert","label":"gt.def5.9.adjoint-hilbert"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces#gt.thm5.11","title":"gt.thm5.11","label":"gt.thm5.11"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/GilbargTrudinger/b